   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#xa0;</p>
   <p style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify;">The deferred day-<em style="font: inherit;">one</em> losses are the difference between the fair value at initial recognition and the transaction price and are amortized pro rata on a straight-line basis until the date of the last expected conversion. For further details in relation to the convertible debentures please refer to note <em style="font: inherit;">7.10.1</em> Financial liabilities overview.</p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#xa0;</p>
