   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#xa0;</p>
   <p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;">At the end of the reporting period and of the previous year, Sono Group had <ix:nonFraction id="c105715991" contextRef="i_2022-12-31" unitRef="EUR" name="sev:TradeAndOtherReceivablesDenominatedInForeignCurrency" scale="3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" decimals="-3">no</ix:nonFraction> trade and other receivables in foreign currencies. There were <em style="font: inherit;">no</em> hedging relationships at the end of the respective periods.</p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#xa0;</p>
   <p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt;">Based on the respective exchange rates, a hypothetical appreciation of the EUR compared to the foreign currencies by <ix:nonFraction id="c105715993" contextRef="d_2022-01-01_2022-12-31_TypesOfRisksAxis-CurrencyRiskMember" unitRef="Pure" name="sev:ForeignExchangeRateHypotheticalAppreciationDepreciation" scale="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" decimals="1">10</ix:nonFraction>% would have resulted in the following effect on consolidated profit or loss before taxes.</p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#xa0;</p>
